The `uptime()` system call could also be made faster by using the shared page. The kernel could store the current number of ticks in the read-only shared page. When a user program needs the uptime, it could read the tick value directly from this page instead of making a system call. This would avoid the user-to-kernel transition and make `uptime()` faster.

